===== Todo 17 (Wave 3): End-to-end MLP correctness + before/after fusion memory-traffic report =====
Date: 2026-07-27
Environment: nix develop --impure --accept-flake-config (llvmPackages_21 MLIR 21.1.8; numpy 2.5.0; pytest 9.0.3; ml_dtypes)

DELIVERABLES CREATED
  tools/polykernel-report/traffic_report.py   analytic before/after fusion memory-traffic CLI
  tools/polykernel-report/mlir_traffic.py     IR -> per-op global-traffic parser (reused by the CLI + the e2e real-file test)
  tools/polykernel-report/polykernel-report   thin executable wrapper (makes the QA command runnable)
  tests/e2e/conftest.py                       e2e fixtures reusing the tests/kernels CPU-ref mechanism + golden harness
  tests/e2e/test_mlp_correctness.py           whole-block e2e correctness (unfused + fused) + negative test + standalone harness
  reports/mlp_traffic.json                    machine-readable traffic report
  reports/mlp_traffic.md                      human-readable traffic report
  reports/w3_e2e_neg.log                      negative-test evidence (broken fused kernel -> non-zero exit)

TRAFFIC MODEL (analytic, not measured)
  traffic(op) = sum(numel(t)*bytes(t) for operand t) + sum(numel(t)*bytes(t) for result t)   # global reads + writes
  fusion saves each eliminated intermediate's global ROUND-TRIP = 2 * numel * bytes (one write + one read removed).
  Eliminated intermediates read from the discardable attrs the fusion passes attach
  (polykernel.fused_from + polykernel.eliminated_type[_N]); polykernel.workspace_bytes (--plan-memory, Todo 16)
  cross-checked (0 for a fused op). before/after totals (sum of per-op traffic over unfused vs fused IR) are
  cross-checked against the sum of eliminated round-trips (they must agree; the tool fails otherwise).

