  Headline (real Llama-2-7B MLP shapes from examples/mlp_block.mlir):
    Before fusion: 478,150,656 bytes (456.00 MiB)
    After fusion:  444,596,224 bytes (424.00 MiB)
    Reduction:      33,554,432 bytes ( 32.00 MiB) = 7.02%
    Consistent (before-after == eliminated round-trips): True

  Per-fused-op breakdown:
    fused_rmsnorm_matmul (fused_from=rmsnorm_matmul) eliminates 32.00 MiB intermediate write+read
    (33,554,432 bytes) from tensor<1x2048x4096xbf16>

  Unfused per-op traffic:                 Fused per-op traffic:
    rmsnorm   reads 16,777,216 writes 16,777,216  traffic 33,554,432     fused_rmsnorm_matmul traffic 152,043,520 workspace 0
    matmul    traffic 152,043,520                                        gelu                 traffic  90,177,536
    gelu      traffic  90,177,536                                        matmul               traffic 152,043,520 workspace 16,777,216
    matmul    traffic 152,043,520                                        add                  traffic  50,331,648
    add       traffic  50,331,648
    TOTAL     478,150,656                                                TOTAL                444,596,224

  Only --fuse-rmsnorm-matmul fires on this block: there is no polykernel.bias op (so --fuse-matmul-bias-gelu
  cannot match the matmul->gelu pair) and the residual add is terminal (so --fuse-residual-rmsnorm has no
  following rmsnorm). The fusion removes the rmsnorm result's global round-trip: written by rmsnorm and read
  back by matmul in the unfused pipeline (2 * 1*2048*4096 * 2 bytes = 32 MiB), kept on-chip when fused.

